A script hook exiting non-zero aborts the transition with exit 2. The script's own stderr is relayed
verbatim ahead of the `error:` line, which names the hook and the exit code it returned. The report
is printed only after every hook has run, so a fault prints no report at all — but the status set is
itself the edge's first hook, so it has already landed on the artifact when a later hook faults.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: never — the hook fails
            hooks: ["script fail-hook"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/fail-hook --
#!/bin/sh
echo "hook says no" >&2
exit 3
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- cmd --
chmod +x ../home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/_scripts/fail-hook
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks intaking --workdir run
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks noted --workdir run
-- exit --
2
-- stdout --
created index.md
not-started → intaking
frontmatter: status=intaking
-- stderr --
hook says no
error: script hook 'fail-hook' exited 3
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: noted
---
